# Federal Program Performance Command Center

A sanitized PL-600 portfolio project demonstrating a centralized federal program-performance, risk-management, forecasting, and executive-reporting solution built with Microsoft Power Platform.

## Project Overview

This solution consolidates program information from disconnected spreadsheets, SharePoint lists, legacy systems, and manual status reports into a centralized program-management and executive-reporting platform.

Program managers can track cost, schedule, performance, risks, issues, milestones, corrective actions, and upcoming deadlines. Leadership receives real-time dashboards and 30-, 60-, and 90-day forecasts for proactive decision-making.

All agencies, programs, users, financial values, and performance metrics in this repository are fictional.

## Business Challenge

Government organizations frequently experience:

- Program data stored across disconnected systems
- Manually prepared weekly and monthly reports
- Inconsistent performance metrics
- Limited visibility into cost and schedule risk
- Delayed identification of missed milestones
- Duplicate and incomplete records
- Difficulty reconciling multiple data sources
- Limited executive-level forecasting
- Dependence on aging legacy systems

## Proposed Solution

The command center provides:

- Centralized program and project tracking
- Cost, schedule, scope, and performance monitoring
- Risk and issue management
- Milestone and deliverable tracking
- Corrective-action management
- Automated data ingestion and validation
- 30-, 60-, and 90-day forecasting
- Role-based data access
- Automated status-report generation
- Executive Power BI dashboards

## Application Modules

### Program Intake

Captures program information, ownership, funding, objectives, dates, stakeholders, and reporting requirements.

### Milestone Management

Tracks milestones, dependencies, responsible owners, planned dates, revised dates, completion status, and supporting documentation.

### Risk and Issue Management

Records program risks and issues, probability, impact, mitigation actions, escalation status, and accountable owners.

### Corrective Action Tracking

Connects performance concerns to corrective actions, milestones, responsible parties, due dates, and completion evidence.

### Executive Reporting

Provides leadership with program health, funding status, milestone performance, overdue actions, risk exposure, and forward-looking forecasts.

